    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented owner registration dates for `POST /api/owners` / `GET /api/owners/{id}`:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. The generator maps `format: date` to `java.time.LocalDate` and serializes it as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, so it now appears in both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response). It's optional, not required.\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `registration_date` mapped column with `LocalDate registrationDate` field plus getter/setter. MapStruct maps it automatically by name in both directions (`OwnerMapper` needed no change).\n\n- **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 the one behavioral rule: after mapping the request to an `Owner`, if no registration date was supplied it defaults to `LocalDate.now()` (the server's current date). A supplied date is preserved.\n\n- **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run against the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL change is what makes persistence work; I updated all four for consistency.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 both `coreDefaultsToToday` (defaults to today when omitted) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (echoes `2020-06-15`) pass, and the full suite is **BUILD SUCCESS** (2 run, 0 failures).",
